# An allow-list, not a deny-list: everything is excluded, and only what the
# Dockerfile copies is added back. A deny-list let `infra/` into the build
# context, so every `az acr build` uploaded prod.tfvars -- the OIDC client
# secret and the session key -- plus 200-odd MB of .terraform into ACR's
# source storage. With this shape, a new file has to be named here before it
# can reach a registry, rather than the other way round.
#
# Beware two dockerignore rules when editing: a pattern without `**` matches
# one path segment only (`*.md` never matches `docs/x.md`), and a directory
# that is excluded is still descended into when a `!` rule below could match
# something inside it.
*

!backend
!analyzer
!frontend

# ...and, under those, what the image has no use for.
backend/data
backend/birdsense
backend/birdsense-analyze
backend/bin
**/__pycache__
